{"event":"tool.finished","payload":{"sessionId":"fix-split","seq":266,"time":1795338134419,"turnId":"turn-245","toolCallId":"call-a8e30aaaf32f","toolName":"Read","outcome":"success","content":[{"type":"text","text":" 1→# tally\n 2→\n 3→Split bills and receipts without losing a cent.\n 4→\n 5→## Install\n 6→\n 7→```\n 8→uv add tally\n 9→```\n10→\n11→## Splitting a bill\n12→\n13→```python\n14→from decimal import Decimal\n15→from tally.money import split_evenly\n16→\n17→split_evenly(Decimal(\"100.00\"), 3)\n18→# [Decimal('33.33'), Decimal('33.33'), Decimal('33.33')]\n19→# Each share is rounded, so the parts can come to 99.99.\n20→```\n21→\n22→## Receipts\n23→\n24→`tally receipt scan photo.jpg` reads a receipt and lists its lines. `tally receipt pdf`\n25→writes a PDF for the group, with each person's share.\n26→\n27→## Multi-currency receipts\n28→\n29→Not yet: every line of a receipt must be in the same currency.\n30→\n31→## Development\n32→\n33→```\n34→uv sync\n35→uv run pytest -q\n36→```\n37→\n38→Licensed under the MIT license."}],"display":{"kind":"file","filePath":"~/code/tally/.dawg/worktrees/split-cents/README.md","startLine":1,"lineCount":38,"totalLines":38,"truncated":false},"durationMs":6}}
